# Peka — Level Design: Act 3 (Twist + Climax — "Into the Light")

> Companion to `game-design.md` / `story.md`. Follows `level-act2.md`.
> The final ascent toward the exit. Act 3 *twists* the core mechanic (gravity is
> no longer fully yours), brings the two halves physically **together** for the
> first time, and ends on the **merge into the light** — the story payoff.
> Still no new movement verbs; the twist is environmental. Impossible solo +
> deterministic/telegraphed throughout (death = full restart, GDD §3).

**Legend** (+ Act 1/2 symbols)
```
⇅ gravity-storm zone (ambient pull inverts on a fixed beat)
✦ light shaft / the exit   ⊕ convergence flip-zone (puts both on one surface)
✜ frozen failed-pair silhouette
```

---

## 3.1 "Gravity Storm" — the twist

Zones where the **ambient pull forcibly inverts both players on a fixed rhythm**
(telegraphed by a visual/audio swell). You can still flip — but the floor you
trusted becomes the ceiling under you. You must *plan around* the storm beat.

```
═══════════════════════════  ⇅⇅⇅ on the beat, "down" flips for BOTH ⇅⇅⇅
   P1 ───jump───▶                 land timing must account for the coming flip
═══════════════════════════
```
- **Solve:** both read the storm beat and pre-commit jumps/flips so the forced inversion lands them safely; one often must be positioned to catch/bridge for the other across an inversion.
- **Impossible solo:** several landings only exist *after* a forced flip, and need a partner-built platform on the surface you'll fall toward.
- **Tests:** mastery of the core mechanic when it's no longer fully under control.

---

## 3.2 "Mirror Lock" — simultaneity gauntlet (peak difficulty)

A chained sequence of **paired switches** that must be struck in **mirrored
timing** across both surfaces; each correct pair shifts geometry to open the next.
The hardest "two bodies, one place, same instant" test in the game.

```
═══◇1══════◇3══════◇5═══   ceiling chain (P2)
═══◇1══════◇3══════◇5═══   floor chain (P1)   hit matching pairs in sync;
   (mistime → geometry resets the sequence; a slip → death → full restart)
```
- **Solve:** P1 & P2 hit ◇1 together, then ◇3, then ◇5, flipping/moving in mirror, no desync.
- **Impossible solo:** simultaneous mirrored input on two surfaces.
- **Tests:** the simultaneity verb at its absolute ceiling; deep partner sync.

---

## 3.3 "Convergence" — the halves meet (story + co-op)

For the **first time**, a flip-zone (⊕) places both halves on the **same surface**.
A stretch they cross *literally together* — adjacent, one boosting/catching the
other in close quarters — foreshadowing the merge. Tonal shift: intimate, quieter.

```
═══════════════════════════
   P1⊕P2 ──together──▶  one short section, side by side / stacked,
═══════════════════════════   close-quarters boosts & catches
```
- **Solve:** stay adjacent; use close boosts/catches that only work shoulder-to-shoulder.
- **Impossible solo:** the section is built for two bodies in contact.
- **Beat:** the wound starting to close — they're nearly whole.

---

## 3.4 "The Failed" — theme peaks (darkest stretch)

A corridor lined with **✜ frozen failed pairs** and the **densest shadow presence**
in the game (the most lost halves). The last and most dangerous gauntlet before
the light — everything the pair has learned, under maximum pressure.

```
✜      ▒   ▒        ✜            walls of reaching silhouettes;
═══════════════════════════     shadows thick on both surfaces;
   P1 ◀threads▶  ▒   ▒   P2      flip-redirect + reach + simultaneity, combined
═══════════════════════════
✜          ▒          ✜
```
- **Solve:** synthesis of all verbs at peak density; the failed pairs telegraph exactly the mistakes that kill.
- **Impossible solo:** layered two-surface dependencies with no static safe route.
- **Theme:** *this is what you become if you let go.* Then — light ahead.

---

## 3.5 "The Light" — CLIMAX & ENDING

The exit. A final **two-body gate**: both halves must stand in opposing
**✦ light-shafts** (one per surface) **at the same moment** to widen the crack.
They step into the light together — and **fold back into one**.

```
              ✦  (the widening crack — the way out)
═══════[P2 in ceiling light-shaft]═══════
              ‖ both lit at once → the crack opens ‖
═══════[P1 in floor light-shaft]═════════
   → both step in → the two halves merge → one being walks out under the sky.
```
- **Solve:** simultaneous presence in both light-shafts (the simultaneity verb, one last time, made sacred).
- **Impossible solo:** the crack needs both lights held at once.
- **Payoff:** the merge (whole again, gravity normal, walks into daylight).
- **Eerie alt:** in the light, **one** shadow where two stood (ambiguous — GDD/story open hook).

